        "original_id": "e0316fea-4b2e-5921-92e8-bad0472592f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Pueraria, Pleiospilos, Pueraria montana\n- Places: Asia, South Africa\n- Concepts: genera, species, hybrids, common names, Aizoaceae\n\nFacts:\n- Pueraria is a genus of 15–20 plant species native to Asia.\n- Pleiospilos is a genus of succulent flowering plants in the Aizoaceae family that is native to South Africa.\n- Pueraria montana is closely related to Pueraria edulis and Pueraria phaseoloides within the genus Pueraria.\n- The common name kudzu is used for Pueraria montana, related Pueraria species, and hybrids between those species.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
